/*******************************************************************************

  	Group:
	typecodes

	Description:
	What (the ??) is a "typecode"?  A typecode is a value that
	is the log-base-2 of the size of a type in bytes.  So, for
	example, the typecode for a 'char' type is '0'.  Why?
	Because the size in bytes of the 'char' type is '1' and the
	value (number base) of two raised to the power of zero ('0')
	is the resulting value of '1', the size in bytes of the
	type 'char'.  OK, so you get the idea.  So the "typecode"
	for the type 'short' is '1', et cetera.  Where are typeocodes
	used or needed?  That is the subject of another explanation.

*******************************************************************************/

module ;

